B. Borwein integrals I_m(t) = int_0^oo (sin tx / x) prod_{j=1}^m sinc(x/(2j+1)) dx = pi/2 - pi*P(S'_m > t)
   F_m(xi) = int_R prod_{j=0}^m sinc(x/(2j+1)) cos(xi x) dx = pi*P(xi-1 <= S'_m <= xi+1)
