  2k = 4   vSC = [2, 3, 5]         excess sum(1/p) - 1 = 1/30       deficit (pi/2 - I)/pi = 1/43200
  2k = 6   vSC = [2, 3, 7]         excess sum(1/p) - 1 = -1/42      deficit (pi/2 - I)/pi = 0
  2k = 8   vSC = [2, 3, 5]         excess sum(1/p) - 1 = 1/30       deficit (pi/2 - I)/pi = 1/43200
  2k = 10  vSC = [2, 3, 11]        excess sum(1/p) - 1 = -5/66      deficit (pi/2 - I)/pi = 0
  2k = 12  vSC = [2, 3, 5, 7, 13]  excess sum(1/p) - 1 = 691/2730   deficit (pi/2 - I)/pi = 74322914521/101569313664000
  => for 2k <= 12 the vSC sinc product is a Borwein integral with excess -B_2k: exact (pi/2) for 2k = 2, 6, 10;
     deficit pi/43200 for 2k = 4, 8; deficit pi*(691^5 - 271^5)/(3840*2730^4) for 2k = 12 (271 = 691 - 420, 420 = 2*2730/13)
  denominators of B_10/20 and B_12/24 (= |im J| in pi_19^s and pi_23^s): 264 = 2^3*3*11 and 65520 = 2^4*3^2*5*7*13
  genus X_0(p) = 0 exactly for p in [2, 3, 5, 7, 13] = {p : (p-1) | 12} = vSC(12)
  {p : (p+1) | 12} = [2, 3, 5, 11] contains {2,3,11}; {p : (p-1) | 12} contains {2,5,7}; {p : (p+1) | 24} = [2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 23] (M24 eta products)
